> those daggers under the other inventory letter and then pick them up again,
> they go back to being under the "b" inventory letter.  (Often, but not
> always.)

     #adjust is working correctly, and these results are predictable.  The
fact that the thrown things you pick back up get placed into a different
inventory slot in the first place is a tip off that they won't merge with
the ones you haven't thrown.  If you want to avoid this, just use 'i' to
look at your inventory at the start of the game, or at least prior to using
#adjust.  As a side effect, you'll know you have precisely 11 or 14 or
whatever daggers instead of "around a dozen". :-}

     The items in your initial inventory aren't marked as having been seen
until you actually look at your inventory.  The ones you pick up off the
ground have been seen.  Seen and unseen objects won't merge together even
if they're otherwise identical.



